israel.description:
At Similarweb, we're revolutionizing the way businesses interact with the digital world by revealing to them everything that happens online. Our cutting-edge platform and unique data empower over 4,300 customers globally, including industry giants like Google, eBay, and Adidas, to make game-changing decisions that drive their digital strategies.

In 2021, we went public on the New York Stock Exchange, and we haven’t stopped growing since!

We're expanding our global presence with a brand-new site in Prague - home to Europe’s top tech talent - and seeking exceptional pioneers to help build a new dynamic team. At Similarweb, you'll innovate fast, collaborate with brilliant minds, solve big problems, work with cutting-edge technologies and data at incredible scales, and make a tangible impact on the world's most innovative companies.

We’re looking for an Experienced Full Stack Developer to design, code and manage Similarweb’s large-scale and highly available services, using cutting edge technologies & design.

The position is within the Incubation team responsible for innovating and developing new Similarweb products, operating with the entrepreneurial spirit and dynamic atmosphere reminiscent of a startup within our organization.

This role will report to Team Manager, R&D.

Here’s what your day will look like:

- Design, code, and manage large-scale, highly available services using cutting-edge technologies.

- Tackle tough problems and find creative ways to solve them.

- Determine feasibility by performing risk management and evaluating tradeoffs.

- Lead decision-making & design of APIs, mechanisms, and abstractions.

- Build new features and directly impact the future of our product end to end (frontend, backend, tests, monitoring, etc.) and cross platforms.

- Write high-quality, functional code – backend and frontend.

- Improve your skills, learn from and mentor top-notch engineers and enrich other team members.

- Perform code reviews, evaluate implementations, and provide feedback.

- Have lots of fun!

Here’s what you’ll need:

- B.Sc. or M.Sc. in Computer Science or a related field;

- 4+ years of previous engineering hands-on experience with web technologies;

- At least 2 years of experience in developing server-side;

- At least 1.5 years of experience in developing front-end/mobile (Well-known frameworks- React, Vue, etc. - an advantage);

- Experience in Typescript;

- Experience in Node.js and at least one large framework(Express, NestJS etc.) in cloud environment (AWS, GCP or Azure);

- Experience with at least one large UI framework (react, angular, vue);

- Experience with databases;

- Experience in architecture and design of production-grade web services;

- Comfortable taking challenges and learning new technologies;

- Excellent communication skills with the ability to provide constant dialog between teams;

- High proficiency in both written and spoken English;

What can you expect?

- Impact😎: Work with the most powerful digital intelligence platform in the world, loved by both customers and employees.

- Innovation🚀: We encourage open dialogue and empower employees to bring their ideas to the table, fostering meaningful change. You’ll find the resources you need to take initiative and create meaningful change within the organization.

- Hybrid Work Model: Enjoy the best of both worlds with our hybrid work model - 3 days in our vibrant office and 2 days working remotely🏡.

- Our Office: Step into our brand new, modern office located in the dynamic DOCK IN area (Prague 8). It's fully equipped with stand desks, comfortable chairs & monitors, designed to inspire focus and collaboration. We've also stocked it with drinks, snacks 🥪, and fruits 🍎and created space for social activities and recreation, making it a vibrant and enjoyable workplace✨.

- Comprehensive Benefits: Your well-being is not just a buzzword! We provide 5 weeks of vacation, an extra day off on your birthday month, sick days, competitive compensation, and much more 😎!

- State of the art tech stack👩🏻‍💻: We adopt innovation and develop using the latest technologies and the best hardware (the latest, most powerful MacBook Pro M3).

- Team events: At Similarweb, we believe in the power of community. That's why we organize team-building events, parties, and company events multiple times a year or weekly, lunches or happy hours 🎉.

- Access to Equity programs💸: share the success of Similarweb by becoming a shareholder in the company.

- You can grow your career in any direction you choose: Interested in becoming a VP or want to transition into a different department? Whether it’s Career Week, personalized coaching, or our ongoing learning solutions, you’ll find all the tools and opportunities you need to develop your career right here🚀.




We will handle your application and information related to your application in accordance with the Applicant Privacy Policy available here.

About Wolt

At Wolt, we create technology that brings joy, simplicity and earnings to the neighborhoods of the world. In 2014 we started with delivery of restaurant food. Now we’re building the delivery of (almost) everything and you’ll find us in over 500 cities in 30 countries around the world. In 2022 we joined forces with DoorDash and together we keep on dreaming big and expanding across the globe.

Working at Wolt isn’t always easy, but it’s definitely exciting. Here you’ll learn more, build more, and ship more than in most other companies. You’ll be challenged a lot, but also have a lot of fun on the way. So, if you’re a self-starter with drive and entrepreneurial spirit, this could be the ride of your life.

What you’ll be doing

We are looking for a highly motivated and data driven Account Specialist to join our growing team.

As an Account Specialist, you’ll play a key role in maximize our partners performance on the Wolt platform. You’ll focus on building strong relationships, providing top tier client experience, and driving growth through data-driven insights and close collaboration with cross-functional teams.

Day-to-day in this role you’ll:

- Partner growth - drive the commercial growth of existing partners;

- Portfolio management - oversee a portfolio of restaurants partners, ensuring value creation across all stakeholders: partners, customers, couriers and Wolt;

- Performance optimization -  use data insights to identify opportunities for partners, propose tailored campaigns and provide high level consultation to boost results;

- Relationship building - act as the key contact for appointed accounts, maintaining strong communication and supporting expansion opportunities;

- Cross-functional collaboration - ensure smooth communication across functions to align goals and optimize partner performance.

Our humble expectations

- 2-3 years of experience in account development, sales; experience in e-commerce or marketplace is a plus;

- Analytical thinking - strategic mindset combined with strong numerical ability to interpret complex data sets and influence decisions at scale;

- Project management - skilled in stakeholder management and process implementation;

- Ownership - proactive, structured and detail - oriented and a “can do” attitude;

- Excellent communication skills, fluency in English;

What we offer

- A fast-growing tech company with lots of career opportunities, both locally and internationally;

- Private Health Insurance;

- FitPass Gym membership;

- Employee Assistance Programme - therapy and wellbeing;

- Employee discount on all Wolt orders;

Next steps

If you're ready to learn, contribute, and grow within a collaborative environment, we’d love to hear from you!

